  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A balloon is moving up in air vertically above a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> on the ground. When it is a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;a&nbsp;girl standing at a distance d (point B) from A (see figure) sees it at an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with respect to the vertical. When the balloon climbs up a further height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, it is seen at an angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with respect to the vertical if the girl moves further by a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>464</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> (point C). Then the height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is (given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5774</mn></math>):</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/2cf70f48-9d4b-465a-8e1e-c3e7c9b8e3b2-image.png\" style=\"width: 303px; height: 228px;\" /></p>",
